# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH (r_e = 1.5949 Angstrom), 6-31G, UCCSD followed by the Lambda equations and the one- and
# two-particle density matrices (CC_RDM TRUE, requires UCCSD TRUE) for all three references: NON_RELATIVISTIC (RHF),
# X2C (X2C-HF) and C4_SPINOR (no-pair DHF). USE_RI (the default) is used for the integrals; USE_RI FALSE (dense) or
# CHOLESKY TRUE work as well.
#
# Output (written next to this file; <name> = lih_uccsd_rdm, with the method appended because three methods run):
#   lih_uccsd_rdm_nonrel.dm1 / .dm2,  lih_uccsd_rdm_x2c.dm1 / .dm2,  lih_uccsd_rdm_4c.dm1 / .dm2
# The report printed after each UCCSD lists the Lambda iterations, the number of elements written, the trace of the 1-RDM
# (the number of electrons) and the energy recomputed from the written elements (sum h gamma + 1/2 sum <pq|rs> Gamma)
# against E_0 + E_c: they agree to ~1e-9 Eh for the default CC_RDM_THRESHOLD 1e-10.
# Read them with   python3 read_cc_rdm.py lih_uccsd_rdm_x2c   (see the docstring there for the record layout: 1-based indices in
# Kramers-pair order, int32 p q [r s] + float64 re im, p<q and r<s in the 2-RDM, terminated by an all-zero record).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
C4_SPINOR TRUE
UCCSD TRUE
CC_RDM TRUE
CC_RDM_THRESHOLD 1e-10

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
